  "history": {
    "claims": [
      {
        "text": "On Rotten Mud Mountain, Ni Jian points two fingers at a brown bear and a burst of sword qi shoots out. The sword qi disperses against the hard plates that a wild defensive Gu raises on the bear’s back, and each strike can only shave off some of its fur. Ni Jian’s grandfather Ni Kun names the weakness of sword qi Gu: it attacks by piercing, and once it is countered, the primeval essence spent on it is wasted with no damage dealt.",
        "chapters": [
          1034
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "intro",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "loc_rotten_mud_mountain",
          "char_ni_jian",
          "sys_defensive_gu",
          "char_ni_kun"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "In Broken Sword Valley, a crowd of Gu Masters charges in after talk of a rank four sword qi Gu. A passerby says the valley may hold only one rank four sword qi Gu. Earlier, someone had found a rank four sword qi Gu, setting off a huge commotion.",
        "chapters": [
          1059
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "stated-rank",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "fac_gu_masters"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Lin Jian Xing’s vital Immortal Gu is rank eight Immortal Gu Sword Qi, the foundation of his killer moves sword qi takes form and sword qi lightning roar. When Prince Feng Xian’s sparks burn his sword qi, his battle foundation is broken.",
        "chapters": [
          2305
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "citation_unchecked",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "holder-and-rank",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "char_lin_jian_xing",
          "sys_immortal_gu",
          "res_sword_qi",
          "char_prince_feng_xian"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Lin Jian Xing’s core Immortal Gu is sword qi Gu. His sword qi is filled with sword path dao marks yet also carries dense qi path dao marks. Heavenly Court restores his killer move sword qi takes form from the sword path dao marks that its immortals brought back from their battle with him. The qi path marks in his sword qi let the restored move target Qi Sea Ancestor, a qi path cultivator, who is struck by it and then sealed.",
        "chapters": [
          2323
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "citation_unchecked",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "qi-path-dao-marks",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "fac_heavenly_court",
          "char_qi_sea_ancestor"
        ]
      }
    ]
